 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Farewell, my dear boy! When haply again\nWe meet thee on that fatiguing journey,\nWhen first I saw thy face and listened\nTo thy lute's tones, the earth shall disappear,\nThe sunbeam relent; for no unrelenting wind\nOf revenge should be with thee to unite,\nNor should thy shuddering heart contrive again\nThou to endure the broken lips again,\nOr sicken when thou dost feel them again.\nThis garb of solitude is ours,\nThy world was but a dream: now alone\nSo oft have we laughed in friendship; alone",
